    "field": "Land use and climate change",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the contradiction where observations show warming from deforestation while climate models show cooling, stemming from observational methods that use a space-for-time assumption, which neglects the crucial, scale-dependent atmospheric feedbacks that are included in coupled simulations.",
    "method": "The proposed methodology uses subgrid-level analysis and filtered coupled climate simulations to separate local biophysical effects from atmospheric feedbacks, thereby reconciling the contradictory temperature responses to deforestation observed in satellite data and models by ensuring a fairer, scale-aware comparison.",
    "task": "The task is to reconcile the disagreement between observed warming and simulated cooling responses to deforestation by comparing satellite data and climate model experiments to understand how scale and atmospheric feedbacks alter local versus large-scale temperature changes.",
